{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The client entry point is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"optional"}]},{"type":"text","value":" out of the box. If not provided, TanStack Start will automatically handle the client entry point for you using the below as a default."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Getting our html to the client is only half the battle. Once there, we need to hydrate our client-side JavaScript once the route resolves to the client. We do this by hydrating the root of our application with the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StartClient"},{"type":"text","value":" component:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/client.tsx\nimport { hydrate } from 'solid-js/web'\nimport { StartClient, hydrateStart } from '@tanstack/solid-start/client'\n\nhydrateStart().then((router) => {\n  hydrate(() => <StartClient router={router} />, document)\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This enables us to kick off client-side routing once the user's initial server request has fulfilled."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-handling","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error Handling"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can wrap your client entry point with error boundaries to handle client-side errors gracefully:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/client.tsx\nimport { StartClient } from '@tanstack/solid-start/client'\nimport { hydrate } from 'solid-js/web'\nimport { ErrorBoundary } from './components/ErrorBoundary'\n\nhydrate(\n  () => (\n    <ErrorBoundary>\n      <StartClient />\n    </ErrorBoundary>\n  ),\n  document.body,\n)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"development-vs-production","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development vs Production"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You may want different behavior in development vs production:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/client.tsx\nimport { StartClient } from '@tanstack/solid-start/client'\nimport { hydrate } from 'solid-js/web'\n\nconst App = (\n  <>\n    {import.meta.env.DEV && <div>Development Mode</div>}\n    <StartClient />\n  </>\n)\n\nhydrate(() => <App />, document.body)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The client entry point gives you full control over how your application initializes on the client side while working seamlessly with TanStack Start's server-side rendering."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"error-handling","text":"Error Handling","level":2},{"id":"development-vs-production","text":"Development vs Production","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> [!NOTE]\n> The client entry point is **optional** out of the box. If not provided, TanStack Start will automatically handle the client entry point for you using the below as a default.\n\nGetting our html to the client is only half the battle. Once there, we need to hydrate our client-side JavaScript once the route resolves to the client. We do this by hydrating the root of our application with the `StartClient` component:\n\n```tsx\n// src/client.tsx\nimport { hydrate } from 'solid-js/web'\nimport { StartClient, hydrateStart } from '@tanstack/solid-start/client'\n\nhydrateStart().then((router) => {\n  hydrate(() => <StartClient router={router} />, document)\n})\n```\n\nThis enables us to kick off client-side routing once the user's initial server request has fulfilled.\n\n## Error Handling\n\nYou can wrap your client entry point with error boundaries to handle client-side errors gracefully:\n\n```tsx\n// src/client.tsx\nimport { StartClient } from '@tanstack/solid-start/client'\nimport { hydrate } from 'solid-js/web'\nimport { ErrorBoundary } from './components/ErrorBoundary'\n\nhydrate(\n  () => (\n    <ErrorBoundary>\n      <StartClient />\n    </ErrorBoundary>\n  ),\n  document.body,\n)\n```\n\n## Development vs Production\n\nYou may want different behavior in development vs production:\n\n```tsx\n// src/client.tsx\nimport { StartClient } from '@tanstack/solid-start/client'\nimport { hydrate } from 'solid-js/web'\n\nconst App = (\n  <>\n    {import.meta.env.DEV && <div>Development Mode</div>}\n    <StartClient />\n  </>\n)\n\nhydrate(() => <App />, document.body)\n```\n\nThe client entry point gives you full control over how your application initializes on the client side while working seamlessly with TanStack Start's server-side rendering.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: client-entry-point\ntitle: Client Entry Point\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> The client entry point is **optional** out of the box. If not provided, TanStack Start will automatically handle the client entry point for you using the below as a default.\n\nGetting our html to the client is only half the battle. Once there, we need to hydrate our client-side JavaScript once the route resolves to the client. We do this by hydrating the root of our application with the `StartClient` component:\n\n```tsx\n// src/client.tsx\nimport { hydrate } from 'solid-js/web'\nimport { StartClient, hydrateStart } from '@tanstack/solid-start/client'\n\nhydrateStart().then((router) => {\n  hydrate(() => <StartClient router={router} />, document)\n})\n```\n\nThis enables us to kick off client-side routing once the user's initial server request has fulfilled.\n\n## Error Handling\n\nYou can wrap your client entry point with error boundaries to handle client-side errors gracefully:\n\n```tsx\n// src/client.tsx\nimport { StartClient } from '@tanstack/solid-start/client'\nimport { hydrate } from 'solid-js/web'\nimport { ErrorBoundary } from './components/ErrorBoundary'\n\nhydrate(\n  () => (\n    <ErrorBoundary>\n      <StartClient />\n    </ErrorBoundary>\n  ),\n  document.body,\n)\n```\n\n## Development vs Production\n\nYou may want different behavior in development vs production:\n\n```tsx\n// src/client.tsx\nimport { StartClient } from '@tanstack/solid-start/client'\nimport { hydrate } from 'solid-js/web'\n\nconst App = (\n  <>\n    {import.meta.env.DEV && <div>Development Mode</div>}\n    <StartClient />\n  </>\n)\n\nhydrate(() => <App />, document.body)\n```\n\nThe client entry point gives you full control over how your application initializes on the client side while working seamlessly with TanStack Start's server-side rendering.\n"}
